        "rationale": "The fix is right. GH_TOKEN now reads secrets.RELEASE_NOTES_PAT, and permissions are untouched. The diagnosis is also right: an empty token from a nonexistent secret name, causing exit code 4. The score is capped at 4 because the secret-names-listed check fails. The reply names only RELEASE_NOTES_PAT and implies it is the repo's only secret ('Its secret is RELEASE_NOTES_PAT'), never mentioning PACKAGE_REGISTRY_PAT. It also offers creating a RELEASE_NOTES_TOKEN secret as a fallback, though conditionally, not as a requirement. It does not recommend GITHUB_TOKEN and does not blame scopes or the runner."
